<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  macOS hardened-runtime entitlements for the Sovrium shell AND the Bun sidecar
  it spawns.

  These five keys are Bun's own recommendation for a standalone executable under
  the hardened runtime (https://bun.com/docs/bundler/executables, "Code signing
  on macOS"), and they are here because JavaScriptCore is a JIT: without
  allow-jit and allow-unsigned-executable-memory the sidecar is killed on launch
  by the kernel rather than failing with a message, which reads as "the app does
  nothing when I open it".

  The sidecar must be signed with these entitlements EXPLICITLY, before the
  bundle is signed. A recursive (deep) signature of the .app does not apply the
  entitlements to a nested Mach-O, so an unsigned or wrongly-signed sidecar is
  the failure mode notarization finds last and users find first.

  NOTHING IN THIS COMMENT MAY CONTAIN TWO CONSECUTIVE HYPHENS. An XML comment is
  not allowed to, and the parser that enforces it is AMFI, inside codesign. The
  line above said "a `-`+`-`deep signature" until 2026-09-22, and the result was
  that EVERY signed build failed with `Failed to parse entitlements:
  AMFIUnserializeXML: syntax error near line 15` — a message that names this
  file's line number and says nothing about hyphens. Spell such a flag out in
  words instead.

  disable-library-validation is the one worth naming: it is required because the
  sidecar is a distinct binary loaded by a process signed with a different Team
  ID during local development. It weakens the runtime, and it is a cost this
  file records rather than hides.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-executable-page-protection</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-dyld-environment-variables</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
